---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/privy-vs-brevo';
const title = 'Privy vs Brevo for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Compare storefront marketing with a Shopify data handoff and a separate transactional-email requirement.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Brevo have a Shopify connection?",
    "answer": "Its current help material describes the Brevo PushOwl app and migration for existing accounts. Check the app and sync rules relevant to your store."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a transactional API replace Shopify notifications?",
    "answer": "Not automatically. Inventory existing notices and deliberately assign each trigger to avoid duplicate service email."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should every European store pair Privy and Brevo?",
    "answer": "No. Choose from the actual marketing, data and service-message requirements, with a separate review of consent and processing arrangements."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Privy vs Brevo</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Privy vs Brevo for Shopify email</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Compare storefront marketing with a Shopify data handoff and a separate transactional-email requirement.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Separate marketing from service messages</h2>
        <p>A multilingual home-goods store might need a welcome offer and a shipment-delay notice. This is a hypothetical planning scenario. Those messages have different purposes and should not share an eligibility rule merely because they use one contact record. Privy presents a combined ecommerce marketing offer; Brevo documents transactional APIs as well as a Shopify connection. That distinction is a useful reason to investigate Brevo, not proof that either product satisfies your complete requirements.</p>
        <h2>Identify the Shopify connector before migrating</h2>
        <p>Brevo documentation now describes the Brevo PushOwl app and migration from an existing Brevo account. Establish which app and account your store uses before following an old Sendinblue setup guide. The migration guide warns that Shopify historical sync can override contact attributes. Export the existing consent and language mappings, decide which system is authoritative, and inspect a limited approved sample before a broad import.</p>
        <h2>Design a locale handoff</h2>
        <p>For the proposed home-goods store, distinguish preferred language from shipping country. A French-speaking customer can order to Germany. Define a fallback for an unknown language and preserve the source of the preference. Preview the welcome offer and service notice in each supported language. Do not infer permission from locale or treat supplier nationality as evidence that your processing arrangement is compliant.</p>
        <h2>Keep transactional ownership explicit</h2>
        <p>List which notices Shopify already sends before introducing an API sender. A shipment-delay event should have an order reference, an intended recipient and a rule preventing duplicate delivery. Ask the implementer to demonstrate retry handling and logging. A replenishment promotion is not automatically transactional because an API sends it. Review message purpose and eligibility separately from the transport.</p>
        <h2>Evaluate capture on comparable terms</h2>
        <p>Use the same offer, placement and audience when considering a different signup surface. Preserve the chosen locale and permission fields through to the first marketing message. Avoid concluding that embedded forms must convert worse than popups without an actual controlled comparison. If Privy remains the capture owner, confirm the specific connector or supported handoff rather than assuming a direct integration.</p>
        <h2>Cost and cutover</h2>
        <p>Quote marketing sends, contact allowance, transactional usage, additional products and implementation work separately. Compare a normal month with a seasonal burst and allow for retry volume on service messages. During a proposed cutover, assign one sender to each notification and journey. Pause the old marketing trigger only when the replacement audience and exclusions are checked; keep an explicit rollback owner.</p>
        <h2>Decision</h2>
        <p>Investigate Brevo when a documented transactional interface or the current Shopify data connection addresses a real requirement. Evaluate Privy against the storefront marketing job it would own. Combining them requires a justified handoff, not an assumption that European operations always need two vendors. Account access, migration behavior and the final processing arrangement still need store-specific verification; this page reports no deployed migration or compliance finding.</p>
        <h2>Primary documentation</h2>
        <p>Product scope checked against primary material on November 25, 2026. Documentation establishes advertised capabilities, not results for this store.</p>
        <ul><li><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/">Privy product scope</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">Current Shopify connection</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://developers.brevo.com/docs/getting-started">Transactional API overview</a></li></ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-mailchimp">Brevo vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-omnisend">Brevo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Privy vs Brevo FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
